# Regression: `data` (the struct-decl keyword) used as a plain variable
# name. It only opens a declaration when a name follows (`data Point:`);
# `data = …` is an ordinary binding. Before, naming a variable `data`
# silently truncated the function body to `ret 0` with no diagnostic.
define main() -> number:
    data = [4, 5, 6]
    print_line("data has {length(data)} items")
    data[0] + data[1] + data[2]   # 15
